Hello,

I have been using the OTG port of my Gumstix Overo Fire in host mode for
quite a while. I'm now trying to get the current kernel from the
linux-omap tree to work, and the USB port is unusable. Exactly what
happens depends on whether I set musb to host or OTG mode in the kernel
config (CONFIG_USB_MUSB_HOST or CONFIG_USB_MUSB_OTG). The full config is
attached, exchanging CONFIG_USB_MUSB_HOST and CONFIG_USB_MUSB_OTG was
the only difference between the kernels in the tests described below.

Kernel source: 2.6.34-rc3, latest commit from
http://git.kernel.org/?p=linux/kernel/git/tmlind/linux-omap-2.6.git
(eba014745cc806d625b6a553d1af6efd14e16321)
plus this patch:
http://git.kernel.org/?p=linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux-2.6.git;a=commit;h=3eac4abaa69949af0e2f64e5c55ee8a22bbdd3e7
("rwsem generic spinlock: use IRQ save/restore spinlocks"; without it,
the Overo won't boot).

When CONFIG_USB_MUSB_HOST is set, I can't load the musb_hdrc module:

# modprobe musb_hdrc debug=1
FATAL: Error inserting musb_hdrc
(/lib/modules/2.6.34-rc3-07875-geba0147-dirty/kernel/drivers/usb/musb/musb_hdrc.ko):
No such device

dmesg shows this:
musb_hdrc: version 6.0, musb-dma, host, debug=1
musb_hdrc musb_hdrc: incompatible Kconfig role setting
musb_hdrc: probe of musb_hdrc failed with error -22

With CONFIG_USB_MUSB_OTG, the module can be loaded.
dmesg output:

musb_hdrc: version 6.0, musb-dma, otg (peripheral+host), debug=1
HS USB OTG: revision 0x33, sysconfig 0x2010, sysstatus 0x1, intrfsel
0x1, simenable  0x0
